well i'm here in la viv ukraine in what  used to be a sporting equipment store  but which has now been transformed into  a volunteer humanitarian center which is  run by a ukrainian ngo called help the  front and as you can see they've got  their hands full they were set up back  in 2014 following the russian annexation  of crimea but they have never been  busier since the russian invasion of  ukraine and of course you know as you  can see they're packed full of boxes a  lot of these containing badly needed  medical supplies these medical kits with  tourniquets and bandages  but they say what they really need is  tactical equipment so  these thermal imaging cameras this  little guy can see body heat through  bushes for example up to one and a half  kilometers away  drones body armor equipment that  ukrainian soldiers desperately need on  the front lines in this collection right  here was in fact recently sent  from canada provided by a group called  maria aid that was just recently set up  by members of the canadian military on a  volunteer basis who previously served  here in ukraine as part of operation  unifier many of the individuals that  they knew on the front lines were  reaching back out to them to say  we need gear we need specialized  equipment we need body armor and helmets  and drones  and so these individuals these  volunteers decided to come together and  form an organization that organization  maria aid was set up in response to the  russian invasion of ukraine and has  since grown to include canadian  paramedics firefighters and ukrainian  canadians from all walks of life they're  now working to send this desperately  needed tactical equipment here to  levieve where it is then distributed to  the front lines jeff semple global news  in la viv ukraine
 

